{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01DqVgYzEUR4WTUivA77g3i1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have read enough papers to write a comprehensive literature review. Now let me also look for datasets and code repositories, then create all the required files. Let me first identify datasets that would be appropriate for this research on multi-agent LLM systems with architectural diversity.\n\nFor this research, the relevant datasets are:\n1. **Reasoning benchmarks** (what the agents would be evaluated on):\n   - GSM8K (math reasoning)\n   - MATH dataset\n   - MMLU (multiple choice knowledge)\n   - StrategyQA\n   - BoolQ\n   - ARC (AI2 Reasoning Challenge)\n   - Knight-Knave-Spy (from Wu 2025 paper - custom dataset)\n\n\n2. **Adversarial and ambiguous tasks** that the paper specifically examines, plus logical reasoning benchmarks like LogiQA and ReClor for evaluating multi-agent performance across diverse knowledge domains. I'll search HuggingFace for the key datasets—GSM8K, MMLU, BoolQ, and StrategyQA—which are all freely available and will form the foundation for testing the agents.\n\nNow I'm identifying the relevant code repositories to work with, including implementations of multi-agent debate frameworks, reconciliation approaches, and agent forest architectures. Let me verify which ones are still accessible and clone them for reference.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3221,"cache_read_input_tokens":63972,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3221,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0dfc82f5-4d11-42d3-841d-877759aeae79","uuid":"c6d188da-2208-4f20-818d-9e8b13db69e6"}
