{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0144jTUSASUvCQSfvcC9Ty7z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0161NDnv6QArzDPCLdskRyH5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspaces/architectural_diversity_in_mul_20260306_214906_8d1e21a6/papers/README.md","content":"# Downloaded Papers\n\nPapers downloaded for \"Architectural Diversity in Multi-Agent LLM Systems for Robust Collective Reasoning\"\n\n## Core Multi-Agent Debate Papers\n\n1. [Du2023_multiagent_debate_factuality.pdf](Du2023_multiagent_debate_factuality.pdf)\n   - **Title**: Improving Factuality and Reasoning in Language Models through Multiagent Debate\n   - **Authors**: Yilun Du, Shuang Li, Antonio Torralba, Joshua Tenenbaum, Igor Mordatch\n   - **Year**: 2023\n   - **arXiv**: 2305.14325\n   - **Why relevant**: Foundational \"society of minds\" multi-agent debate paper; homogeneous agents baseline\n\n2. [Liang2023_divergent_thinking_debate.pdf](Liang2023_divergent_thinking_debate.pdf)\n   - **Title**: Encouraging Divergent Thinking in Large Language Models through Multi-Agent Debate\n   - **Authors**: Tian Liang, Zhiwei He, Wenxiang Jiao et al.\n   - **Year**: 2023\n   - **arXiv**: 2305.19118\n   - **Why relevant**: Introduces MAD framework; identifies DoT problem; code available for experiments\n\n3. [Chan2023_chateval_multiagent_evaluators.pdf](Chan2023_chateval_multiagent_evaluators.pdf)\n   - **Title**: ChatEval: Towards Better LLM-based Evaluators through Multi-Agent Debate\n   - **Authors**: Chi-Min Chan et al.\n   - **Year**: 2023\n   - **arXiv**: 2308.07201\n   - **Why relevant**: Multi-agent evaluation framework; debate for quality assessment\n\n4. [Chen2023_reconcile_diverse_llms.pdf](Chen2023_reconcile_diverse_llms.pdf)\n   - **Title**: ReConcile: Round-Table Conference Improves Reasoning via Consensus among Diverse LLMs\n   - **Authors**: Justin Chih-Yao Chen, Swarnadeep Saha, Mohit Bansal\n   - **Year**: 2023\n   - **arXiv**: 2309.13007\n   - **Why relevant**: MOST DIRECTLY RELEVANT - heterogeneous multi-model framework; proves diversity critical\n\n5. [Wu2025_can_llm_agents_debate.pdf](Wu2025_can_llm_agents_debate.pdf)\n   - **Title**: Can LLM Agents Really Debate? A Controlled Study of Multi-Agent Debate in Logical Reasoning\n   - **Authors**: Haolun Wu, Zhenkun Li, Lingyao Li\n   - **Year**: 2025\n   - **arXiv**: 2511.07784\n   - **Why relevant**: Controlled ablation of diversity vs. other factors; Knight-Knave-Spy dataset\n\n## LLM Ensemble and Diversity Papers\n\n6. [Survey2025_llm_ensemble.pdf](Survey2025_llm_ensemble.pdf)\n   - **Title**: Harnessing Multiple Large Language Models: A Survey on LLM Ensemble\n   - **Authors**: Zhijun Chen et al.\n   - **Year**: 2025\n   - **arXiv**: 2502.18036\n   - **Why relevant**: Comprehensive taxonomy of all ensemble methods; reference survey\n\n7. [Diverse2025_llms_ensembling.pdf](Diverse2025_llms_ensembling.pdf)\n   - **Title**: Diverse LLMs or Diverse Question Interpretations? That is the Ensembling Question\n   - **Authors**: Rafael Rosales, Santiago Miret (Intel Labs)\n   - **Year**: 2025\n   - **arXiv**: 2507.21168\n   - **Why relevant**: Questions model diversity effectiveness; compares model vs. prompt diversity\n\n8. [Stable2025_llm_ensemble_diversity.pdf](Stable2025_llm_ensemble_diversity.pdf)\n   - **Title**: Stable LLM Ensemble: Interaction between Example Representativeness and Diversity\n   - **Authors**: Junichiro Niimi\n   - **Year**: 2025\n   - **arXiv**: 2510.13143\n   - **Why relevant**: Optimal diversity calibration; temperature + example selection\n\n9. [LLM_TOPLA2024_ensemble_diversity.pdf](LLM_TOPLA2024_ensemble_diversity.pdf)\n   - **Title**: LLM-TOPLA: Efficient LLM Ensemble by Maximising Diversity\n   - **Authors**: Selim Furkan Tekin et al. (Georgia Tech)\n   - **Year**: 2024\n   - **arXiv**: 2410.03953\n   - **Why relevant**: Focal diversity metric; diversity-optimized ensemble pruning; learn-to-ensemble\n\n10. [More2024_agents_all_you_need.pdf](More2024_agents_all_you_need.pdf)\n    - **Title**: More Agents Is All You Need\n    - **Authors**: Junyou Li et al. (Tencent)\n    - **Year**: 2024\n    - **arXiv**: 2402.05120\n    - **Why relevant**: Key homogeneous ensemble baseline; Agent Forest scaling behavior\n\n## Heterogeneous Ensemble and Robustness\n\n11. [Wu2023_heterogeneous_ensemble_robustness.pdf](Wu2023_heterogeneous_ensemble_robustness.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Exploring Model Learning Heterogeneity for Boosting Ensemble Robustness\n    - **Authors**: Yanzhao Wu, Ka-Ho Chow, Wenqi Wei, Ling Liu (Georgia Tech)\n    - **Year**: 2023\n    - **arXiv**: 2310.02237\n    - **Why relevant**: Formal analysis of heterogeneous ensemble robustness via negative correlation\n\n## Multi-Agent Frameworks\n\n12. [Hong2023_metagpt.pdf](Hong2023_metagpt.pdf)\n    - **Title**: MetaGPT: Meta Programming for A Multi-Agent Collaborative Framework\n    - **Authors**: Sirui Hong et al.\n    - **Year**: 2023\n    - **arXiv**: 2308.00352\n    - **Why relevant**: Key multi-agent framework reference; role-based agent coordination\n\n13. [Sumers2023_cognitive_architectures_agents.pdf](Sumers2023_cognitive_architectures_agents.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Cognitive Architectures for Language Agents\n    - **Authors**: Theodore R. Sumers et al.\n    - **Year**: 2023\n    - **arXiv**: 2309.02427\n    - **Why relevant**: Comprehensive survey of agent architectures; design space for diversity\n\n## Reasoning Surveys\n\n14. [Li2025_system2_reasoning_survey.pdf](Li2025_system2_reasoning_survey.pdf)\n    - **Title**: From System 1 to System 2: A Survey of Reasoning Large Language Models\n    - **Authors**: Zhong-Zhi Li et al.\n    - **Year**: 2025\n    - **arXiv**: 2502.17419\n    - **Why relevant**: Contextualizes collective reasoning in the reasoning landscape\n\n15. [Adversarial2025_robustness_llms.pdf](Adversarial2025_robustness_llms.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Benchmarking Adversarial Robustness to Bias Elicitation in Large Language Models\n    - **Authors**: Multiple authors\n    - **Year**: 2025\n    - **arXiv**: 2504.07887\n    - **Why relevant**: Adversarial robustness benchmarking; bias elicitation methods for testing\n\n## Additional Papers\n\n16. [SWEDebate2025_competitive_debate.pdf](SWEDebate2025_competitive_debate.pdf)\n    - **Title**: SWE-Debate: Competitive Multi-Agent Debate for Software Issue Resolution\n    - **Year**: 2025 | arXiv: 2507.23348\n\n17. [TreeOfDebate2025_multipersona.pdf](TreeOfDebate2025_multipersona.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Tree-of-Debate: Multi-Persona Debate Trees Elicit Critical Thinking\n    - **Year**: 2025 | arXiv: 2502.14767\n\n18. [TSDebate2026_multimodal_debate.pdf](TSDebate2026_multimodal_debate.pdf)\n    - **Title**: TS-Debate: Multimodal Collaborative Debate for Zero-Shot Time Series Reasoning\n    - **Year**: 2026 | arXiv: 2601.19151\n\n19. [Enterprise2024_multigenai_collaboration.pdf](Enterprise2024_multigenai_collaboration.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Towards Effective GenAI Multi-Agent Collaboration\n    - **Year**: 2024 | arXiv: 2412.05449\n\n20. [Narrative2025_llm_collaborate.pdf](Narrative2025_llm_collaborate.pdf)\n    - **Title**: The Power of Stories: Narrative Priming Shapes How LLM Agents Collaborate\n    - **Year**: 2025 | arXiv: 2505.03961\n\n21. [ExpertReasoning2026_llm_collaborative.pdf](ExpertReasoning2026_llm_collaborative.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Requesting Expert Reasoning: Augmenting LLM Agents with Learned Collaborative Interventions\n    - **Year**: 2026 | arXiv: 2602.22546\n\n22. [VendiRAG2025_diversity_quality.pdf](VendiRAG2025_diversity_quality.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Vendi-RAG: Adaptively Trading-Off Diversity And Quality\n    - **Year**: 2025 | arXiv: 2502.11228\n\n23. [MultiLLM2024_agent_tool_learning.pdf](MultiLLM2024_agent_tool_learning.pdf)\n    - **Title**: Small LLMs Are Weak Tool Learners: A Multi-LLM Agent\n    - **Year**: 2024 | arXiv: 2401.07324\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequ